      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This is Japanese blues stripped to its physical essentials: Komoto's voice and harmonica against Uchida's guitar, with no rhythm section or arrangement machinery to hide behind. Their live identity depends on pressure, timing, call-and-response and improvisational friction, and Billboard's small-room format should make that interaction unusually visible. The first Billboard Live run gives the setting a real reason to pay attention without pretending the Tokyo date is a once-only event.",
